# yq2 -- filtering a multi-document file
#
# `kubectl get -o yaml` and most repos keep several resources in one file,
# separated by `---`. yq runs the expression once per document, and
# `select(cond)` drops the documents where cond is false.
#
# Task: print the name of every Deployment that runs 2 or more replicas,
# one per line. For manifests.yaml that is:
#   api
#   web
#
# The check runs `yq -N --from-file query.yq manifests.yaml` (-N: no `---`
# separators in the output).
#
# The expression below matches nothing at all, and it has no replica filter
# yet. Kinds are case-sensitive, and conditions combine with `and`.
#

select(.kind == "deployment") | .metadata.name
